      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.11 AZLX-23-000215"
      info        : "Amazon Linux 2023 must disable access to network bpf system call from nonprivileged processes.

GROUP ID: V-274004RULE ID: SV-274004r1120000

Loading and accessing the packet filters programs and maps using the bpf() system call has the potential of revealing sensitive information about the kernel state."
      solution    : "Configure Amazon Linux 2023 to prevent privilege escalation through the kernel by disabling access to the bpf syscall by adding the following line to a file, in the \"/etc/sysctl.d\" directory:

kernel.unprivileged_bpf_disabled = 1

The system configuration files must be reloaded for the changes to take effect. To reload the contents of the files, run the following command:

$ sudo sysctl --system"
