    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.175 AZLX-23-002520"
      info        : "Amazon Linux 2023 must allocate an audit_backlog_limit of sufficient size to capture processes that start prior to the audit daemon.

GROUP ID: V-274168RULE ID: SV-274168r1120492

Without the capability to generate audit records, it would be difficult to establish, correlate, and investigate the events relating to an incident or identify those responsible for one.

If auditing is enabled late in the startup process, the actions of some startup processes may not be audited. Some audit systems also maintain state information only available if auditing is enabled before a given process is created.

Audit records can be generated from various components within the information system (e.g., module or policy filter).

Allocating an audit_backlog_limit of sufficient size is critical in maintaining a stable boot process. With an insufficient limit allocated, the system is susceptible to boot failures and crashes.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000254-GPOS-00095, SRG-OS-000341-GPOS-00132"
      solution    : "Configure Amazon Linux 2023 to allocate sufficient audit_backlog_limit to capture processes that start prior to the audit daemon with the following command:

$ sudo grubby --update-kernel=ALL --args=audit_backlog_limit=8192"
      reference   : "800-53|AU-4,800-53|AU-14(1),800-53r5|AU-4,800-53r5|AU-14(1),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001464,CCI|CCI-001849,CSF|PR.DS-4,CSF|PR.PT-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.6,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.15,ITSG-33|AU-4,ITSG-33|AU-14,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.3.1,NESA|T3.6.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-274168r1120492_rule,STIG-ID|AZLX-23-002520,SWIFT-CSCv1|6.4,Vuln-ID|V-274168"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26107"
      cmd         : "/sbin/grubby --info=ALL | /bin/grep args | /bin/grep 'audit_backlog_limit' | /bin/awk -F'audit_backlog_limit=' '{print $2}' | /bin/awk '{gsub(/[^0-9]/,\"\"); print}'"
      expect      : "^(819[2-9]|8[2-9][0-9]{2}|9[0-9]{3}|[1-9][0-9]{4,})$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.176 AZLX-23-002535"
      info        : "Amazon Linux 2023 must enable discretionary access control on hardlinks.

GROUP ID: V-274169RULE ID: SV-274169r1120495

By enabling the fs.protected_hardlinks kernel parameter, users can no longer create soft or hard links to files they do not own. Disallowing such hardlinks mitigates vulnerabilities based on insecure file system accessed by privileged programs, avoiding an exploitation vector exploiting unsafe use of open() or creat().

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00123, SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"
      solution    : "Configure Amazon Linux 2023 to enable DAC on hardlinks with the following:

Add or edit the following line in a system configuration file in the \"/etc/sysctl.d/\" directory:

fs.protected_hardlinks = 1

Load settings from all system configuration files with the following command:

$ sudo sysctl --system"
      reference   : "800-171|3.1.1,800-171|3.1.7,800-171r3|03.01.02,800-171r3|03.01.07a.,800-53|AC-3(4),800-53|AC-6(10),800-53r5|AC-3(4),800-53r5|AC-6(10),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-002165,CCI|CCI-002235,CN-L3|7.1.3.2(b),CN-L3|7.1.3.2(g),CN-L3|8.1.4.2(d),CN-L3|8.1.4.2(f),CN-L3|8.1.4.11(b),CN-L3|8.1.10.2(c),CN-L3|8.1.10.6(a),CN-L3|8.5.3.1,CN-L3|8.5.4.1(a),CSF|PR.AC-4,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.AA-05,CSF2.0|PR.DS-10,CSF2.0|PR.IR-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.15,ISO-27001-2022|A.5.33,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.2,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.3,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.18,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.20,ISO/IEC-27001|A.9.4.1,ISO/IEC-27001|A.9.4.5,ITSG-33|AC-3(4),ITSG-33|AC-6,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T4.2.1,NESA|T5.1.1,NESA|T5.2.2,NESA|T5.4.1,NESA|T5.4.4,NESA|T5.4.5,NESA|T5.5.4,NESA|T5.6.1,NESA|T7.5.2,NESA|T7.5.3,NIAv2|AM1,NIAv2|AM3,NIAv2|AM23f,NIAv2|SS13c,NIAv2|SS15c,NIAv2|SS29,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|7.1.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|7.2.1,PCI-DSSv4.0|7.2.2,QCSC-v1|3.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-274169r1120495_rule,STIG-ID|AZLX-23-002535,SWIFT-CSCv1|5.1,TBA-FIISB|31.1,TBA-FIISB|31.4.2,TBA-FIISB|31.4.3,Vuln-ID|V-274169"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26107"
      cmd         : "/sbin/sysctl fs.protected_hardlinks"
