    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.182 AZLX-23-002575"
      info        : "Amazon Linux 2023 must prevent the loading of a new kernel for later execution.

GROUP ID: V-274177RULE ID: SV-274177r1120519

Changes to any software components can have significant effects on the overall security of Amazon Linux 2023. This requirement ensures the software has not been tampered with and that it has been provided by a trusted vendor.

All software packages must be signed with a cryptographic key recognized and approved by the organization.

Verifying the authenticity of software prior to installation validates the integrity of the software package received from a vendor. This verifies the software has not been tampered with and that it has been provided by a trusted vendor."
      solution    : "Configure Amazon Linux 2023 to disable kernel image loading.

Add or edit the following line in a system configuration file in the \"/etc/sysctl.d/\" directory:

kernel.kexec_load_disabled = 1

Load settings from all system configuration files with the following command:

$ sudo sysctl --system"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.5,800-171r3|03.04.05,800-53|CM-5(3),800-53r5|CM-14,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-003992,CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.2,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.4,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.19,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.31,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.32,ITSG-33|CM-5(3),LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.2.3,NESA|T5.1.1,NESA|T5.6.1,NESA|T7.5.1,NESA|T7.5.3,NESA|T7.6.3,QCSC-v1|7.2,Rule-ID|SV-274177r1120519_rule,STIG-ID|AZLX-23-002575,Vuln-ID|V-274177"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26107"
      cmd         : "/usr/sbin/sysctl kernel.kexec_load_disabled"
      expect      : "^[\\s]*kernel\\.kexec_load_disabled[\\s]*=[\\s]*1[\\s]*$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.183 AZLX-23-002580"
      info        : "Amazon Linux 2023 must prevent files with the setuid and setgid bit set from being executed on the /boot/efi directory.

GROUP ID: V-274178RULE ID: SV-274178r1120522

The \"nosuid\" mount option causes the system not to execute \"setuid\" and \"setgid\" files with owner privileges. This option must be used for mounting any file system not containing approved \"setuid\" and \"setguid\" files. Executing files from untrusted file systems increases the opportunity for nonprivileged users to attain unauthorized administrative access."
      solution    : "Configure Amazon Linux 2023 so that the /boot/efi directory is mounted with the \"nosuid\" option.

Modify \"/etc/fstab\" to use the \"nosuid\" option on the \"/boot/efi\" directory."
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-53|CM-7(2),800-53r5|CM-7(2),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001764,CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7(2),LEVEL|2A,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-274178r1120522_rule,STIG-ID|AZLX-23-002580,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-274178"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26107"
      file        : "/etc/fstab"
      regex       : "^[^#\\n\\r]+[\\s]+/boot/efi[\\s]+"
      expect      : "^[^#\\n\\r]+[\\s]+/boot/efi[\\s]+[^#\\n\\r]+nosuid"
    </custom_item>

