      expect      : "^Manual Review Required$"
      severity    : MEDIUM
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.37 AZLX-23-001090"
      info        : "Amazon Linux 2023 must manage excess capacity, bandwidth, or other redundancy to limit the effects of information flooding types of denial-of-service (DoS) attacks.

GROUP ID: V-274030RULE ID: SV-274030r1120078

DoS is a condition when a resource is not available for legitimate users. When this occurs, the organization either cannot accomplish its mission or must operate at degraded capacity.

Managing excess capacity ensures that sufficient capacity is available to counter flooding attacks. Employing increased capacity and service redundancy may reduce the susceptibility to some DoS attacks. Managing excess capacity may include, for example, establishing selected usage priorities, quotas, or partitioning."
      solution    : "Configure Amazon Linux 2023 to manage excess capacity, bandwidth, or other redundancy to limit the effects of information flooding types of DoS attacks.

Configure \"nftables\" to be the default \"firewallbackend\" for \"firewalld\" by adding or editing the following line in \"etc/firewalld/firewalld.conf\":

FirewallBackend=nftables

Establish rate-limiting rules based on organization-defined types of DoS attacks on impacted network interfaces."
      reference   : "800-53|SC-5(2),800-53r5|SC-5(2),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001095,CSF|PR.DS-4,CSF2.0|DE.CM-01,CSF2.0|PR.IR-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.6,ITSG-33|SC-5(2),LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.3.1,NIAv2|GS8e,NIAv2|GS10c,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-274030r1120078_rule,STIG-ID|AZLX-23-001090,SWIFT-CSCv1|6.4,Vuln-ID|V-274030"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26107"
      file        : "/etc/firewalld/firewalld.conf"
      regex       : "(?i)^[\\s]*FirewallBackend[\\s]*="
      expect      : "(?i)^[\\s]*FirewallBackend[\\s]*=[\\s]*nftables[\\s]*$"
    </custom_item>

