      see_also        : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26107"
      file            : "/etc/ssh/sshd_config /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/*"
      regex           : "^(?i)[\\s]*PubkeyAuthentication[\\s]+"
      expect          : "^(?i)[\\s]*PubkeyAuthentication[\\s]+\"?yes\"?[\\s]*$"
      required        : NO
      min_occurrences : "1"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type            : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description     : "1.55 AZLX-23-001235"
      info            : "Amazon Linux 2023 SSHD must not allow blank passwords.

GROUP ID: V-274048RULE ID: SV-274048r1120132

If an account has an empty password, anyone could log on and run commands with the privileges of that account. Accounts with empty passwords must never be used in operational environments.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000106-GPOS-00053, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00229"
      solution        : "Configure Amazon Linux 2023 to prevent SSH users from logging on with blank passwords.

Edit the following line in \"etc/ssh/sshd_config\" or in a file in \"/etc/ssh/sshd_config.d\":

PermitEmptyPasswords no

Restart the SSH daemon for the settings to take effect:

$ sudo systemctl restart sshd.service"
