    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.80 AZLX-23-002045"
      info        : "Amazon Linux 2023 must take action when allocated audit record storage volume reaches 95 percent of the audit record storage capacity.

GROUP ID: V-274073RULE ID: SV-274073r1120207

If action is not taken when storage volume reaches 95 percent utilization, the auditing system may fail when the storage volume reaches capacity."
      solution    : "Configure Amazon Linux 2023 to initiate an action when allocated audit record storage volume reaches 95 percent of the repository maximum audit record storage capacity by adding/modifying the following line in the /etc/audit/auditd.conf file.

admin_space_left = 5%"
      reference   : "800-171|3.3.4,800-171r3|03.03.04,800-53|AU-5(1),800-53r5|AU-5(1),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001855,CN-L3|7.1.3.7(e),CSF|PR.PT-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ITSG-33|AU-5(1),LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.3.1,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-274073r1120207_rule,STIG-ID|AZLX-23-002045,TBA-FIISB|37.3.2,Vuln-ID|V-274073"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26107"
